/// `halt` signals a `Halt`, which is resumable: handled with `resume:`, the
/// value answers from `halt` and execution carries on after it. Unhandled,
/// its `defaultAction` -- the hook the debugger will replace -- ends the
/// run, reporting the class name, since it has no text.
class HaltResumesWhenHandledAndEndsTheRunWhenNot = Object new () (
  public main: platform args: arguments = (
    |
      transcript = platform transcript.
      Halt = platform kernel Halt.
    |
    transcript
        show: ([
          self halt.
          3.
        ] on: Halt do: [:e | e resume: 7]) printString;
        newLine.
    transcript
        show: ([self halt] on: Halt do: [:e | e resume: 7]) printString;
        newLine.
    self halt.
    transcript
        show: 'not reached';
        newLine.
  )
)
